# Content Extraction Rules

Rules for extracting and sanitizing webpage content. Reference [src/extension/content.js](mdc:src/extension/content.js) for implementation.

## Extraction Strategy

Five-strategy fallback system:

1. Site-specific (Twitter/X status pages)
2. Article element (`main article`, `article`)
3. Content selectors (`.post-content`, `.article-content`)
4. Largest text container
5. Full body (last resort)

## Site-Specific Handling

### Twitter/X
- Extract main tweet only
- Selector: `[data-testid="tweetText"]`
- Exclude: Replies, timeline, engagement metrics

### News Sites
- Extract article body
- Metadata: Author, date, headline
- Remove: Ads, navigation, comments

### Blogs
- Extract post content
- Preserve: Structure, headings
- Remove: Sidebars, widgets

### Documentation
- Extract headings and content
- Preserve: Code blocks, structure
- Remove: Navigation, footer

### Forums
- Extract thread content
- Metadata: Thread title, participants
- Remove: Signatures, timestamps

### E-commerce
- Extract product information
- Metadata: Product name, price, availability
- Remove: Related products, reviews

## Sanitization Pipeline

Three-layer process:

### 1. DOM Cleaning
```javascript
ContentSanitizer.cleanDOM(element)
```
- Removes: Scripts, styles, iframes, ads, navigation
- Preserves: Text content, structure

### 2. Text Cleaning
```javascript
ContentSanitizer.cleanText(text)
```
- Removes: Noise patterns, engagement metrics
- Filters: Empty lines, duplicate content
- Preserves: Meaningful text

### 3. AI Preparation
```javascript
ContentSanitizer.prepareForAI(text, maxLength=8000)
```
- Removes: URLs, emails
- Truncates: Intelligently at sentence boundary
- Formats: Clean whitespace

## Content Limits

- Maximum length: 8000 characters
- Truncation: At sentence boundary
- Minimum meaningful: 50 characters
- Fallback: Use full body if extraction fails

## Return Format

```javascript
{
  success: boolean,
  content: string, // Structured content with metadata
  error?: string
}
```

## Structured Content Format

```
---SITE TYPE---
{siteType}
---PAGE TITLE---
{pageTitle}
---PAGE URL---
{pageUrl}
---METADATA---
{metadata}
---PAGE CONTENT---
{mainContent}
```

## Error Handling

- Protected pages: chrome:// pages return error
- No content: Return error with helpful message
- Extraction failure: Try fallback strategies
- Final fallback: Return body content with warning

## IIFE Wrapper

Content script wrapped in IIFE to prevent redeclaration errors:

```javascript
(function() {
  // extraction code
  return extractAndReturnContent();
})();
```

## Prohibited Patterns

- No eval() or dynamic code execution
- No modifying page DOM (read-only)
- No external API calls from content script
- No storing sensitive page data
